# Operator minimal input (hard contract)

**Scope:** Email processing agent chat only.

## Operator may type (only)

| Input | When |
|-------|------|
| **login** | Once per session start |
| **RE** | **First case of session only** |
| **PR** | Each non-transfer EMAIL case — pastes reply |
| **DONE** | End of workday |
| **BRIEF** (optional) | During a CALL — provides KB/TM context; does not gate Auto-LF |
| Reiteration / correction | Any case — agent updates reply/LF for **this Fall # only** (case exception; does **not** overwrite TM/KB/rules — `.cursor/rules/operator-case-exceptions.mdc`) |

**Physical Sprinklr clicks** (Anwenden, Weiter, Next, Senden, Speichern, transfer UI) are **not** chat commands.

## Forbidden operator commands (never ask for these)

**NEXT**, **RE** (case 2+), **LF**, **LF TR**, **RE SHOW**, **pickup**, **await**, or any "type X to continue".

If automation stalls, agent **fixes internally** — never push work back to the operator.

---

## Full case lifecycle (agent handles everything)

### Monitoring window
Active only between **arm click** (Anwenden/Weiter/Next) and **new case sidetray click**.
Hook (`extract_auto_continue_hook.py`) and sidetray poll run only during this window. Silent everywhere else.

### EMAIL case

```
[Monitoring: arm fired → sidetray click]
  → agent clicks sidetray item (CASE_ITEM_AUTO_CLICKED)
  → case opens → extract → 7-step visible in chat (automatic, no operator RE)
  → Auto-LF → --closeout-anwenden (background, monitoring disarmed)
  → agent rests, awaiting:
      PR  (operator pastes reply)              → paste + verify → PR done for #FALL_ID
      reiteration (change reply / LF)          → agent updates → stays resting
      arm fires (Anwenden without PR, edge)    → [monitoring active] → next case
  → operator clicks Anwenden → arm fires → [monitoring active] → next case
```

### CALL case

```
[Monitoring: arm fired → case pops up (no click)]
  → CHANNEL: CALL → Auto-LF voice
  → --closeout-next/weiter/extern (background, monitoring disarmed)
  → agent rests, awaiting:
      BRIEF  (operator pastes call context) → KB/TM lookup, talk-track — no new LF
      arm fires (Next/Weiter)               → [monitoring active] → next case
```

### Transfer (EMAIL or CALL)

```
  Auto-LF TR → --closeout-weiter/extern (background)
  → agent rests
  → operator completes transfer UI → arm fires → [monitoring active] → next case
  (no PR)
```

---

## Arm timing (critical — changed from previous rule)

**Arm starts at Auto-LF time, not at PR time.**

| Case | When `--closeout-*` starts |
|---|---|
| EMAIL non-transfer | **Immediately after Auto-LF** (before PR) |
| EMAIL transfer | Immediately after Auto-LF TR |
| CALL | Immediately after Auto-LF voice |

**PR (EMAIL non-transfer):** Agent just pastes the reply. Arm is already running. No arm command at PR time.

---

## Stop hook backup

`.cursor/hooks/extract_auto_continue_hook.py` fires `[AUTO_PIPELINE]` only during the monitoring window (`monitoring_armed.json = true`). Silent outside it — no false flags during wait-for-PR.

## Transfer / CALL

- Transfer Auto-LF → `--closeout-weiter` or `--closeout-extern` — no PR.
- CALL Auto-LF → `--closeout-next` — no PR unless operator provides BRIEF and requests a reply.
